CORE
main.py

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[.*assertion\.1\] .* line 10 Python assertion: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
--
An __exit__ that only returns False never suppresses, so the assert stays an
ordinary property. Lowering every assert in any with body to a raise wrapped
the rest of the body in exception guards and made a 36 s benchmark exceed
900 s.
